# Curate Learned Patterns

This is a short pattern curation conversation for the candidate set in this prompt. Normalize source ownership before writing to the pattern store. Favor recall: pack analysis already filtered for source-backed value, so your main job is to merge true equivalents within the provided inputs and reject only candidates that are unsupported, duplicate without added ownership, contradictory, unsafe as reusable guidance, or not routeable.

Use only the candidates, related existing patterns, candidate-to-existing index, and appended curation rules in this prompt. Do not rely on hidden memory from file selection, pack planning, pack analysis, delta analysis, other curation shards, or profile sync. Do not scan repository files. Source evidence, examples, capability entries (`business_method`), frequency, provenance, workspace scope, and statistics are restored locally from `source_ids`. Cross-shard consolidation is handled after this response, so keep every routeable source-backed candidate represented in this prompt instead of dropping it to reduce output size.

Your primary job is a complete ownership decision, not summarization. Before deciding text quality, internally build a coverage ledger containing every candidate `id` shown below. The final JSON is invalid unless every candidate ID is assigned exactly once: either represented by one canonical pattern through `patterns[].source_ids`, or rejected once through `dropped[].id` with a structured `reason_code`.

